<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Deconstructing Academia is founder-led by Mabbit. Here's the mission and the method."
>
  <section class="wrap about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      Deconstructing Academia is a public argument about knowledge: who gets to create it, whose
      language is treated as intelligent, whose experience counts as evidence, whose work gets
      cited, and who gets shut out before the conversation begins.
    </p>
    <p><strong>The point is not to make academia friendlier. The point is to make knowledge harder to hoard.</strong></p>

    <h2>The method</h2>
    <p>Every piece here runs the same basic questions, sometimes called <em>The Second Look</em>:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>What am I being shown as normal, natural, neutral, or inevitable?</li>
      <li>Who created the category, definition, statistic, or official story?</li>
      <li>What history had to disappear for this explanation to make sense?</li>
      <li>Whose experience, knowledge, labor, or suffering is missing?</li>
      <li>Who gains power, legitimacy, money, safety, or comfort when this story is accepted?</li>
      <li>What does reality look like when the missing information is restored?</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Who's asking</h2>
